WEBVTT

00:01.780 --> 00:04.450
Wow, the Healers' Guild. It's been a while.

00:04.450 --> 00:08.570
Even though I'm a healer, I've been at 
the Adventurers' Guild the whole time.

00:13.080 --> 00:16.560
Um, Kururu-san, it's very nice to see you.

00:16.560 --> 00:20.320
Oh, Luciel-kun. What did you come here for?

00:20.320 --> 00:22.780
I c-came for my renewal.

00:22.780 --> 00:24.540
<i>She's in a real bad mood!</i>

00:24.540 --> 00:29.590
Ever since you took Monika to the Adventurers' 
Guild, I've been trying to hire new help.

00:29.590 --> 00:32.500
But nobody's come, so it's been really tough.

00:35.250 --> 00:38.100
<i>She doesn't seem to be very busy, though.</i>

00:38.100 --> 00:41.650
Well, at least Monika-san's life 
is no longer in danger.

00:41.650 --> 00:42.930
I guess you're right.

00:43.390 --> 00:46.150
Renewal, right? Give me your card.

00:46.150 --> 00:47.350
Sure.

00:47.520 --> 00:48.940
Wait here a minute.

00:51.070 --> 00:55.070
H-Hey, Luciel-kun?! 
What's going on with you?

00:55.070 --> 00:56.480
What kind of risky training...

00:56.480 --> 00:59.030
I mean, where and what kind 
of a life have you been living?

00:59.430 --> 01:02.620
I-I've been living at 
the A-Adventurers' Guild!

01:02.620 --> 01:04.120
What?

01:08.510 --> 01:12.760
<b>The Great Cleric</b>

01:09.590 --> 01:12.760
A Salaryman's <b>Path </b>to <b>Surviving Another World</b>

02:36.140 --> 02:40.010
#5 The Healing Clinic and the Arrival of Bottaculli

02:36.790 --> 02:38.720
Tell me what that's all about!

02:43.580 --> 02:45.800
And that's how I spent the year.

02:45.800 --> 02:50.190
Luciel-kun, are you some 
kind of weirdo? A masochist?

02:47.890 --> 02:50.600
<b>Weirdo</b>

02:49.390 --> 02:50.600
<b>Masochist</b>

02:50.600 --> 02:54.580
I simply wanted to improve my 
self-defense skills, so I don't get killed.

02:54.580 --> 02:57.820
I thought practical 
training would be the best way

02:57.820 --> 02:59.700
to raise my holy magic affinity level.

02:59.700 --> 03:04.010
But you could do that at a clinic! 
You'd even get paid for it.

03:04.550 --> 03:09.410
What's most important for new healers is 
getting experience and practicing treatment.

03:09.410 --> 03:13.030
Also, I think healing just for the money

03:13.030 --> 03:18.090
and receiving a fee for satisfactory 
treatment are two different things.

03:19.010 --> 03:21.540
<i>That's why that happened to Monika-san.</i>

03:22.290 --> 03:25.500
<i>Because the Healers' Guild has 
neglected to keep things under control.</i>

03:26.410 --> 03:30.310
My goal for this year was 
to learn to defend myself.

03:30.310 --> 03:33.100
That is something you cannot buy with money.

03:34.310 --> 03:36.980
I guess you're right. I apologize.

03:36.980 --> 03:39.490
No, I should apologize! 
I'm sorry to sound so arrogant.

03:39.490 --> 03:40.820
That's all right.

03:40.820 --> 03:42.600
Also, Kururu-san...

03:43.530 --> 03:46.390
I am definitely not any kind 
of weirdo or masochist!

03:47.160 --> 03:50.000
You sure are ambitious, Luciel-kun.

03:50.000 --> 03:50.790
Gulp!

03:51.150 --> 03:54.380
Anyway, I can raise you to Rank C, 
but what do you want to do?

03:54.380 --> 03:56.320
The offering gets more expensive,

03:54.380 --> 04:03.470
<b>Rank F</b>

03:56.320 --> 03:59.000
but you'll be able to buy 
the spell tome for Cure at rank F,

03:56.500 --> 04:07.810
<b>Rank E</b>

03:58.500 --> 04:07.810
<b>Rank D</b>

03:59.000 --> 04:03.470
Middle Heal at E, Barrier 
at D, and Area Heal at C.

04:00.510 --> 04:07.810
<b>Rank C</b>

04:03.470 --> 04:05.620
And how much would that cost?

04:05.620 --> 04:07.790
That would be 90 silver coins.

04:07.790 --> 04:09.890
<i>90 silver coins?!</i>

04:09.890 --> 04:13.270
<i>Is the Healers' Guild headquarters 
the real money-grubber around here?</i>

04:13.270 --> 04:16.770
<i>And considering the offering, 
I wonder how much it'll add up to.</i>

04:16.770 --> 04:20.600
<i>I figure that one-third of my income 
goes to rent when living alone,</i>

04:20.600 --> 04:22.780
<i>and then there are living expenses...</i>

04:24.240 --> 04:28.990
<i>I guess I need to find a job. 
I'll ask her about some clinics.</i>

04:28.990 --> 04:30.620
Um, Kururu-san—

04:31.530 --> 04:36.580
I'll give you one gold coin to transfer 
Luciel to the Adventurers' Guild for one year.

04:37.210 --> 04:40.490
I'll even pay him for it. 
I'll give you wages.

04:40.490 --> 04:42.210
Instructor B-Brod?

04:42.210 --> 04:43.380
What are you doing here?

04:43.890 --> 04:46.970
I forgot to hand you your earnings.

04:47.530 --> 04:48.150
Luciel.

04:48.150 --> 04:49.430
Y-Yes, sir?

04:49.430 --> 04:53.330
I want you to become a regular 
resident of the Adventurers' Guild.

04:53.330 --> 04:54.270
Huh?

04:57.530 --> 05:00.020
I'm still trying to hit you, Instructor.

05:00.020 --> 05:03.690
But if there's pay involved, 
I think that sounds ideal.

05:04.030 --> 05:04.950
Then it's decided.

05:04.950 --> 05:08.460
Luciel-kun! Are you sure about this? Really?

05:08.460 --> 05:11.040
I've been studying martial arts 
with the Instructor.

05:11.430 --> 05:14.220
He's a trustworthy person. 
I don't feel threatened.

05:14.840 --> 05:17.380
I'll accept the transfer 
to the Adventurers' Guild.

05:19.250 --> 05:22.050
Very well. I'll allow it.

05:24.670 --> 05:27.400
Phew. Guess I'm back home.

05:27.400 --> 05:29.230
I sure did get teased for it, though.

05:29.230 --> 05:30.530
Change your mind already?

05:30.530 --> 05:32.020
Back so soon?

05:32.020 --> 05:33.640
Ah, shh!

05:33.640 --> 05:40.110
Well, I got a new spell tome, so I'll try 
to learn as much magic as I can in a year.

05:41.460 --> 05:42.570
Yes?

05:43.290 --> 05:45.190
Let's go get dinner, Luciel.

05:45.190 --> 05:46.760
All right!

05:46.760 --> 05:50.840
<i>First, I've got to at least get 
strong enough to be able to travel.</i>

05:57.810 --> 05:59.260
Whoa!

05:59.260 --> 06:00.890
Yeah!

05:59.650 --> 06:02.340
Our healer makes his appearance!

06:02.800 --> 06:03.860
There he is!

06:04.090 --> 06:06.270
What are you so surprised about?

06:06.270 --> 06:08.630
Starting today, you're a temporary employee.

06:08.630 --> 06:10.510
Of course there's a welcome party!

06:10.510 --> 06:12.710
Hey, Luciel! Here you g—

06:12.710 --> 06:13.970
Gross!

06:15.610 --> 06:18.020
There it is! Substance X!

06:16.770 --> 06:17.480
Ew.

06:18.020 --> 06:19.080
That reeks!

06:18.430 --> 06:20.090
<i>Everyone's running away!</i>

06:19.080 --> 06:20.440
What a stench!

06:21.080 --> 06:23.390
Um, do I still have to drink that?

06:23.390 --> 06:28.450
Of course you do. The party can't 
get started until you toast with this.

06:29.260 --> 06:31.280
I'll let you lead the toast.

06:31.280 --> 06:32.200
Huh?

06:32.780 --> 06:36.750
Well then, I hate to be presumptuous, 
but please allow me to lead everyone in a toast.

06:36.750 --> 06:39.610
The Adventurers' Guild 
has been my home for a year

06:39.610 --> 06:41.460
and has already given me many memories.

06:41.780 --> 06:44.940
Some wonderful memories, 
and some unpleasant ones.

06:44.940 --> 06:48.990
I hope you adventurers all make it back home,
even if you're on the verge of death.

06:48.990 --> 06:52.470
Guild employees, I hope you can 
bear with me for yet another year.

06:52.470 --> 06:55.560
Well then, let's drink to 
your fortune and happiness.

06:55.560 --> 06:56.650
Cheers!

06:56.650 --> 06:58.520
Cheers!

07:08.070 --> 07:09.610
Oh, sick.

07:09.610 --> 07:11.490
He really is a masochist.

07:11.840 --> 07:14.580
He's gonna ruin his taste and smell!

07:16.830 --> 07:18.290
<b>Belch</b>

07:17.170 --> 07:20.260
<i>I wish Gulgar-san and the rest 
had to drink this, too!</i>

07:25.370 --> 07:27.820
<i>I smell so bad, everyone's avoiding me.</i>

07:27.820 --> 07:30.680
Yo, Luciel. You reek, man.

07:30.680 --> 07:31.600
Bazan-san?

07:31.600 --> 07:34.050
You really can't escape the stench.

07:34.050 --> 07:36.050
Sekiroth-san and Basura-san?

07:36.450 --> 07:38.680
Hey, can I ask you something?

07:38.680 --> 07:39.640
Sure.

07:40.070 --> 07:42.360
Are you actually... into guys?

07:43.730 --> 07:45.110
Huh?!

07:45.110 --> 07:48.230
I mean, you're always training, you know,

07:48.230 --> 07:52.150
and even when you're with the receptionists, 
you never make a move on them.

07:52.150 --> 07:55.170
If I did make a move, Instructor 
Brod would hunt me down!

07:55.170 --> 07:56.620
Yeah, I guess you're right.

07:56.620 --> 08:00.660
Plus, for the last year, I was concentrating 
on raising the survival rates,

08:00.660 --> 08:02.530
so there wasn't any time for that.

08:04.190 --> 08:08.510
The last place I lived didn't have 
people walking around with weapons,

08:08.510 --> 08:11.600
so for the first six months here, 
I was always on edge.

08:11.550 --> 08:15.810
That

08:11.600 --> 08:13.840
Even though you have the guts to drink that?

08:13.840 --> 08:16.310
Well, at least it doesn't kill me.

08:16.920 --> 08:18.060
I guess you're right.

08:18.490 --> 08:23.100
<i>That time I bumped into Bazan-san, 
I felt like my soul had left me.</i>

08:23.580 --> 08:27.500
When surrounded by adventurers,
all I could see in my future was death.

08:27.500 --> 08:29.570
And coming from a zombie like you...

08:30.070 --> 08:34.780
Well, the way you are now, I don't think 
anybody in this town will mess with you.

08:35.280 --> 08:36.990
D-Do you think so?

08:36.990 --> 08:39.930
Yeah. But if anything happens, come to us.

08:39.930 --> 08:41.580
Oh. Okay!

08:41.580 --> 08:44.220
That's right. Don't be shy.

08:44.220 --> 08:45.720
Sekiroth-san.

08:45.720 --> 08:47.400
By the way, Luciel-kun.

08:47.400 --> 08:48.090
Hmm?

08:48.540 --> 08:51.040
Are you really sure you like girls?

08:51.040 --> 08:52.970
Why do you keep bugging me about that?

08:53.460 --> 08:57.740
In that case, next time I'll take 
you out to enjoy the night life.

08:57.740 --> 08:58.580
Huh?

09:00.310 --> 09:03.380
Th-Th-There are shops 
like that here in the city?

09:03.380 --> 09:05.100
Oh, that got your attention?

09:05.100 --> 09:08.680
But you stick out, Luciel, so 
I bet people are gonna talk.

09:08.680 --> 09:10.590
It's only innocent curiosity.

09:11.690 --> 09:13.190
Luciel-sama?

09:14.700 --> 09:16.530
I'm very glad you came back.

09:16.530 --> 09:17.910
Monika-san?

09:17.910 --> 09:20.660
<i>She didn't hear all that, did she?</i>

09:20.990 --> 09:23.310
How was the Healers' Guild?

09:23.310 --> 09:25.810
Kururu-san seemed to have time on her hands.

09:25.810 --> 09:27.870
Oh, is that right?

09:28.260 --> 09:31.750
By the way, Monika-san, are you 
still glad you came here?

09:31.750 --> 09:37.350
Yes! I get to spend a lot of time 
with adventurers and you, Luciel-sama,

09:37.350 --> 09:40.100
and it feels like the days just fly by.

09:40.630 --> 09:43.870
It's all thanks to you saving me.

09:44.490 --> 09:46.060
Thank you very much!

09:51.850 --> 09:54.190
Oh dear, I found a split end.

09:52.430 --> 09:54.610
Ah! Oopsie!

09:54.610 --> 09:56.560
What's up with those two?

09:56.560 --> 09:58.230
Enjoying the spring of their lives.

09:58.230 --> 09:59.480
They sure are young.

10:01.510 --> 10:03.240
What is this all about?

10:03.650 --> 10:08.510
Our income and our number of slaves 
are half of what they were last year?!

10:08.510 --> 10:10.070
Th-The truth is,

10:10.070 --> 10:13.670
it has something to do with a healer 
affiliated with the Adventurers' Guild.

10:13.670 --> 10:14.670
Hmm?

10:14.670 --> 10:16.930
A healer, you say?

10:28.230 --> 10:29.630
Ow. Ouch.

10:29.630 --> 10:31.530
Ah, I cannot allow that!

10:31.530 --> 10:32.400
Quit your squawking.

10:32.400 --> 10:34.530
Who do you think I am?

10:34.530 --> 10:35.480
Wait!

10:36.980 --> 10:39.070
All right, which one is it.

10:40.280 --> 10:42.520
I've spotted him. Over there.

10:42.520 --> 10:43.370
Hmm?

10:43.930 --> 10:46.440
So you're the healer living in this Guild?

10:46.440 --> 10:48.330
Yes. Yes, I am.

10:48.700 --> 10:51.290
Hmph. What an impudent brat.

10:51.600 --> 10:53.040
Who are you?

10:53.040 --> 10:56.250
If you don't know that, you're also ignorant.

10:56.250 --> 10:58.080
Listen here.

10:58.500 --> 11:03.150
I am the one and only head 
of the strongest clinic in Merratoni.

11:03.150 --> 11:04.850
I'm Bottaculli!

11:04.850 --> 11:06.940
Bottaculli...

11:07.740 --> 11:08.520
Oh!

11:08.520 --> 11:12.730
What kind of healer would 
do something like this?

11:12.730 --> 11:15.690
It believe it was Bottaculli-san.

11:16.240 --> 11:18.650
<i>The guy who tried to kill Monika!</i>

11:19.050 --> 11:21.970
I'm giving you a direct order.

11:21.970 --> 11:27.160
You're going to quit healing at the 
Adventurers' Guild and come work at my clinic!

11:27.160 --> 11:28.330
I refuse.

11:28.330 --> 11:30.170
Wh-What did you say?

11:30.170 --> 11:34.130
I'm here on an official transfer 
from the Healers' Guild.

11:34.130 --> 11:37.110
I'm giving you a direct order out of mercy.

11:37.110 --> 11:39.970
What makes you think you can turn it down?

11:39.970 --> 11:45.220
"Mercy" is not about making threats 
and forcing someone to lose their job.

11:45.220 --> 11:46.500
How dare you!

11:46.500 --> 11:49.810
But why would I go to your 
clinic in the first place?

11:49.810 --> 11:52.750
Ever since you came to this Guild,

11:52.750 --> 11:56.890
the number of patients visiting 
my clinic has dropped off a cliff!

11:56.890 --> 11:59.200
A clinic is a place to save lives.

11:59.200 --> 12:02.610
What kind of patient would go to 
a place with such a horrible reputation?

12:03.420 --> 12:06.780
Are you telling me my clinic 
has a bad reputation?

12:08.210 --> 12:10.000
<i>It's pretty clear it does.</i>

12:10.000 --> 12:12.890
And yet, you're by far my senpai as a healer,

12:12.890 --> 12:15.460
and the head of the 
biggest clinic in Merratoni.

12:15.860 --> 12:19.480
As such, I wonder if I could ask you 
to teach me something, Bottaculli-san.

12:19.480 --> 12:20.170
Oh?

12:21.470 --> 12:24.430
I'll hear you out. I am 
by far your senpai, after all.

12:24.430 --> 12:25.920
<i>That was easy.</i>

12:25.920 --> 12:28.010
Well then, I will ask.

12:28.010 --> 12:30.010
When patients have bone 
fractures or severe illnesses,

12:30.010 --> 12:33.350
what kind of magic do you use 
at your clinic, Bottaculli-san?

12:34.290 --> 12:35.520
Get a load of this.

12:35.520 --> 12:40.770
I use High Heal! And at the 
unprecedented price of 30 gold coins!

12:36.730 --> 12:44.610
<b>High-Level
Recovery
Magic</b>

12:38.730 --> 12:44.610
<b>30 Gold
Coins!</b>

12:40.770 --> 12:42.330
That is unprecedented.

12:42.330 --> 12:43.400
I know, right?

12:43.400 --> 12:44.610
I mean in a bad way.

12:45.080 --> 12:49.450
Then, if it's something like 
a forest wolf bite that draws blood?

12:49.450 --> 12:51.690
High Heal, obviously!

12:51.690 --> 12:55.510
And then, if the patient 
doesn't have the money to pay?

12:55.510 --> 12:58.130
I won't tell you that so easily.

12:58.130 --> 13:01.840
But I do have ways to get 
all the money I'm owed.

13:01.840 --> 13:05.550
By selling them to slave traders 
in other countries? Is that it?

13:06.910 --> 13:10.530
If it's a light wound, wouldn't Heal 
or Middle Heal be enough to save them?

13:10.530 --> 13:14.030
What would be the point 
of using such low-level magic now?

13:14.030 --> 13:17.650
What do I care if the patients' 
pockets are full or not?

13:17.650 --> 13:20.610
They come to the clinic to get saved, right?

13:20.910 --> 13:24.150
Why should I get complaints 
after saving them? Why?!

13:24.150 --> 13:27.080
<i>He sure said that like he meant it!</i>

13:27.080 --> 13:31.960
<i>Is that how this guy built up 
the biggest clinic in Merratoni?</i>

13:32.540 --> 13:35.760
Why don't you use more appropriate 
treatments to save more patients

13:35.760 --> 13:36.830
and earn money that way?

13:36.830 --> 13:39.720
We healers are not slaves.

13:39.720 --> 13:43.800
Why should I spend time on work 
that doesn't earn me money?

13:43.800 --> 13:46.050
That kind of work will 
only earn you resentment!

13:46.050 --> 13:49.400
And yet, don't you believe that 
recovery magic is a gift from God

13:49.400 --> 13:52.150
that is meant to help people?

13:54.050 --> 13:57.020
You're too green. You're too green, kid.

13:57.020 --> 14:00.370
I feel like I'm looking at my old self.

14:01.230 --> 14:06.470
I bet you've never been attacked 
for trying your very best to treat someone

14:06.470 --> 14:12.020
with recovery spells when you've 
already completely run out of magic.

14:12.020 --> 14:15.700
<i>This man trained enough to 
be able to use High Heal.</i>

14:16.370 --> 14:20.140
<i>He may have once been a healer 
who was respected by the people.</i>

14:20.140 --> 14:23.400
<i>If so, he may still have 
some goodness left inside.</i>

14:24.280 --> 14:28.260
If it ever came to that point, 
I might lose faith in humanity.

14:28.260 --> 14:29.260
Right?

14:29.620 --> 14:31.620
I won't do you wrong.

14:31.620 --> 14:34.080
If you know what's good 
for you, come to my place—

14:33.300 --> 14:34.080
However...

14:34.080 --> 14:34.820
Oh?

14:35.200 --> 14:38.700
Were you always only surrounded by enemies?

14:39.390 --> 14:41.770
Did you have no allies at all?

14:41.770 --> 14:44.510
Have you never considered that 
the people you've sold into slavery

14:44.510 --> 14:47.740
have families of their own?

14:47.740 --> 14:50.530
You don't know what 
you're talking about, punk!

14:50.530 --> 14:53.950
If you are able to recite High Heal, 
then you must have great powers!

14:54.240 --> 14:56.110
But if patients won't see you despite that,

14:56.110 --> 14:59.370
can't you see that there's 
a problem with your management?

14:59.370 --> 15:02.550
The way you work only brings about misery!

15:03.340 --> 15:05.470
I'm through with you.

15:05.470 --> 15:07.670
Now you've really made me mad.

15:07.670 --> 15:10.350
You, over there! Kill him now!

15:11.130 --> 15:12.890
I'd like to see you try!

15:15.100 --> 15:16.220
Instructor Brod!

15:17.950 --> 15:24.790
Lord Bottaculli, how much misfortune has 
your business practices caused until now?

15:25.470 --> 15:27.690
Maybe I should take 
a very close look into that!

15:32.930 --> 15:34.200
Get the hell out of here!

15:34.200 --> 15:35.760
Y-Yes, sir!

15:36.160 --> 15:38.450
Thank you very much, Instructor!

15:38.450 --> 15:40.100
You just saved my life.

15:40.100 --> 15:43.420
I never expected Bottaculli 
to set his sights on you.

15:43.420 --> 15:48.160
Yes, well, I still have a feeling 
he was once a good healer.

15:51.700 --> 15:55.770
There have been some troublemakers 
asking around about you.

15:56.180 --> 16:00.100
I haven't done anything shady, 
so I don't care about that at all.

16:00.100 --> 16:05.320
<i>I've only been here for a little over a year.
No way anyone would have anything on me.</i>

16:05.770 --> 16:10.340
But some out there may come after you 
to win favor with Bottaculli.

16:11.070 --> 16:12.920
<i>Why? Is that even fair?</i>

16:12.920 --> 16:16.950
That's why, starting today, 
I'm done training you as a healer.

16:17.830 --> 16:21.350
Starting today, I'll train you the same 
as new gladiators and knights.

16:21.350 --> 16:22.700
A Spartan education!

16:23.090 --> 16:25.470
Um, I'm only a healer.

16:25.470 --> 16:26.790
Don't worry.

16:26.790 --> 16:29.470
All I'll do is train you 
twice as hard as before

16:29.470 --> 16:32.220
and increase your meal 
and Substance X portions.

16:33.150 --> 16:35.510
<i>That makes me do nothing </i>but<i> worry!</i>

16:35.790 --> 16:38.570
There are times when 
a man must do what he can.

16:38.570 --> 16:41.390
Do you think that's going to convince me?

16:41.390 --> 16:43.980
If you don't want to die, 
then shut up and obey!

16:43.980 --> 16:46.310
Y-Yes, sir!

16:50.640 --> 16:53.240
Stand up! Show me you can land one hit on me!

17:01.040 --> 17:01.950
Squeeze

17:04.660 --> 17:06.670
That must've killed him.

17:07.400 --> 17:08.400
He's still alive?!

17:10.180 --> 17:11.630
Here I go!

17:11.630 --> 17:12.630
Come on!

17:15.840 --> 17:16.490
Take that!

17:16.490 --> 17:20.720
Uuugh

17:16.490 --> 17:20.720
Uuugh

17:16.490 --> 17:20.720
Th-This guy is a healer maso-zombie!

17:21.490 --> 17:23.310
Who are you calling a maso-zombie?!

17:23.310 --> 17:26.450
Oh, Maso? Aren't you zombie-ing today?

17:26.450 --> 17:27.850
Here, too?

17:27.850 --> 17:30.050
We'll join in on the training, too.

17:30.050 --> 17:32.030
Might not be as masochistic as you, though.

17:32.030 --> 17:34.550
Let's work hard without becoming zombies!

17:34.550 --> 17:36.160
Yeah!

17:37.510 --> 17:41.240
Now that I think of it, it seems like 
more people are training these days.

17:41.240 --> 17:45.710
You're having an effect, Luciel-sama. 
They want to follow your example.

17:45.710 --> 17:48.530
Survival rates have increased as well.

17:48.530 --> 17:50.150
Huh.

17:50.150 --> 17:53.230
<i>So then what's this maso-zombie crap?</i>

17:53.800 --> 17:58.330
Hey, Luciel. You can already use 
barrier-type defensive spells, right?

17:58.330 --> 17:59.200
Yes, sir.

17:59.200 --> 18:01.220
Okay. Cast one for me.

18:01.220 --> 18:02.140
Yes, sir!

18:02.610 --> 18:03.990
Attack Barrier!

18:04.520 --> 18:05.310
Huh?

18:06.730 --> 18:11.440
Hmm. I threw you pretty hard, but you 
aren't dead and aren't unconscious.

18:12.210 --> 18:13.600
Nothing broken, right?

18:13.600 --> 18:15.400
What was that, all of a sudden?

18:15.400 --> 18:18.350
I figured you wouldn't die 
with the barrier activated.

18:18.350 --> 18:20.320
But there must be a better way.

18:20.670 --> 18:22.680
I gave you some warning, right?

18:22.680 --> 18:25.910
There is such a thing as a surprise attack.

18:25.910 --> 18:28.870
Then this isn't training anymore.

18:28.870 --> 18:30.170
Yeah. You're right.

18:30.170 --> 18:31.040
Huh?

18:31.430 --> 18:34.070
Up to now, you've been training.

18:34.070 --> 18:36.710
You didn't die and you 
didn't take too much damage.

18:37.380 --> 18:40.500
But starting today, we're adding 
more pain to the program.

18:40.500 --> 18:41.640
What?

18:41.640 --> 18:42.950
Use this.

18:42.950 --> 18:43.720
Huh?

18:43.720 --> 18:44.670
Just do it.

18:44.670 --> 18:45.850
Y-Yes, sir!

18:50.410 --> 18:54.150
<i>It's the real thing. Does that 
mean this is a real fight now?</i>

18:54.150 --> 18:57.770
Am I really in such bad shape?

18:57.770 --> 18:59.330
No, not at all.

18:59.330 --> 19:00.110
Huh?

19:00.110 --> 19:03.860
Over the last year, we built up 
your physical foundation.

19:04.250 --> 19:06.050
You don't have any weird habits.

19:06.050 --> 19:10.340
You also aren't naturally gifted, 
but we can keep working on that.

19:10.340 --> 19:14.170
With materials like that, of course 
I'd want to make you an apprentice.

19:14.170 --> 19:15.800
A-Apprentice?

19:15.800 --> 19:19.200
From now on, I'll train you as my apprentice.

19:19.200 --> 19:21.010
You can start calling me Master.

19:21.010 --> 19:23.640
Y-Yes, Master Brod!

19:23.640 --> 19:27.000
And one more thing. 
Until I say it's okay,

19:27.000 --> 19:30.190
you're forbidden from checking 
your status and skill levels.

19:30.190 --> 19:31.240
Huh?

19:31.240 --> 19:34.110
<i>That's the one thing that 
was keeping me motivated!</i>

19:34.110 --> 19:35.820
Of course, there's a good reason.

19:35.820 --> 19:38.500
If you're only chasing after the numbers,

19:38.500 --> 19:41.530
you'll lose sight of what 
it takes to become powerful.

19:41.810 --> 19:46.530
No matter how high your status gets, if your 
head is chopped off your body, you're dead.

19:46.900 --> 19:50.970
Even at your current level, if you thrust your
sword into my neck with my guard down,

19:50.970 --> 19:52.290
I'm dead.

19:52.720 --> 19:57.460
Guys obsessed with status are 
useless when push comes to shove.

19:58.110 --> 20:02.170
<i>I wonder if there was a time when 
even Master was obsessed with status.</i>

20:02.630 --> 20:03.640
I understand.

20:03.640 --> 20:08.250
Good! This time I won't take you by 
surprise, so put up a good barrier!

20:08.250 --> 20:09.140
Yes, sir!

20:09.500 --> 20:14.080
<i>Once I make it through this training, 
I'm sure I'll have a more peaceful life ahead.</i>

20:14.080 --> 20:17.410
Once you're used to it, try to imagine 
seeing yourself and your enemy

20:17.410 --> 20:19.110
fighting from a bird's-eye view.

20:19.110 --> 20:21.410
I have to get that far into the zone?

20:22.720 --> 20:27.030
<i>There's a huge gap between the level of 
performance he wants from me and where I am now.</i>

20:27.510 --> 20:30.390
<i>But still, I have to trust him.</i>

20:30.810 --> 20:34.110
<i>Instead of running, I have to land a blow!</i>

20:34.510 --> 20:39.180
<i>I'm still where I was when 
I started training a year ago.</i>

20:40.260 --> 20:43.760
Just so you know, I'm praying 
that you don't run away.

20:43.760 --> 20:45.430
I will give it my all!

20:48.230 --> 20:51.430
That's how I spent six days 
a week in this world.

20:51.430 --> 20:54.230
On the Day of Wind and Sun, 
martial arts and fighting.

20:54.230 --> 20:56.660
On the Day of Fire, 
swordsmanship and shielding.

20:56.660 --> 20:58.410
On the Day of Water, spearmanship.

20:58.410 --> 21:00.610
On the Day of Earth, throwing and archery.

21:00.610 --> 21:04.030
And on the Day of Darkness, 
scholarship and magic training.

21:04.030 --> 21:05.870
I started working hard to improve myself.

21:10.000 --> 21:13.790
Bottaculli-sama, here is 
the report about that healer.

21:14.330 --> 21:17.310
One silver coin for one hour of treatment?

21:17.310 --> 21:22.570
It's guys like this who 
make me look like I'm greedy!

21:22.570 --> 21:25.900
What the hell is wrong with using 
the skills I was blessed with

21:25.900 --> 21:28.140
to try to become wealthy?!

21:28.140 --> 21:30.100
That damn hypocrite!

21:31.140 --> 21:32.560
Oh. I know.

21:33.520 --> 21:38.100
"The healer named Luciel-san is 
charging absurd prices for treatment

21:38.440 --> 21:40.820
and trying to interfere with my business.

21:41.130 --> 21:43.560
However, he does seem talented,

21:43.560 --> 21:46.400
so I'd like you to promote him 
to a position elsewhere."

21:48.020 --> 21:50.530
At least I'm not lying. There's no lie here.

21:50.990 --> 21:54.310
Take this to the head of the Healers' Guild.

21:54.310 --> 21:55.640
Understood.

21:57.240 --> 22:00.670
This way, even if he realizes 
I'm the one who transferred him,

22:00.670 --> 22:02.940
it won't leave a mark on my reputation.

22:02.940 --> 22:07.010
Oh well! I guess I can put up 
with it for one year.

22:22.040 --> 22:24.410
Ah, my throat!

23:55.690 --> 23:59.210
Bottaculli-san sure is a nasty guy, right?

23:59.210 --> 24:01.030
Luciel-kun told me that where he's from,

24:01.030 --> 24:05.210
after someone like that leaves, 
you "throw salt" for purification.

24:01.370 --> 24:02.790
Tear Ducts Destroyed

24:05.210 --> 24:06.840
Next time: On a Journey.

24:05.210 --> 24:09.970
#6 On a Journey

24:06.840 --> 24:09.920
Gulgar-san, please bring 
a whole barrel of salt!
